==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|fr|cor anglais|lit=English horn}}, calqued from a misunderstanding of {{etyl|gmh|en}} {{m|gmh|[[engel]]lisches [[horn]]||angelic horn}}, from the resemblance of the instrument to horns played by angels as depicted in the Middle Ages.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cor anglais}}

# {{l|en|A double [[reed]] [[woodwind]] [[instrument]] in the [[oboe]] family that is [[pitch]]ed in [[F]], a fifth lower than the oboe and is consequently approximately one-third [[long]]er than the oboe.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|English horn}}

